        "headline": "Tornado Warning issued October 11 at 11:32AM EDT until October 11 at 12:15PM EDT by NWS Wilmington NC",
        "description": "TORILM\n\nThe National Weather Service in Wilmington has issued a\n\n* Tornado Warning for...\nSouth Central Columbus County in southeastern North Carolina...\nCentral Horry County in northeastern South Carolina...\n\n* Until 1215 PM EDT.\n\n* At 1132 AM EDT, a severe thunderstorm capable of producing a\ntornado was located over Adrian, or 7 miles northeast of Conway,\nmoving northeast at 35 mph.\n\nHAZARD...To …[trimmed]",
        "instruction": "Move to an interior room on the lowest floor of a well-built building\naway from windows. If you are outdoors, in a mobile home, or in a\nvehicle, move to the closest substantial shelter and protect yourself\nfrom flying debris.\n\nPlease send your reports of hail or wind damage by calling the\nNational Weather Service office in Wilmington at 1 800 697 3901.",
